@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if [[ "$#" -lt 2 ]]; then
+  echo "usage: run_logged.sh LOG COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 64
+fi
+
+log="$1"
+shift
+{
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+  "$@"
+  status="$?"
+  printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %s\n' "$status"
+  exit "$status"
+} 2>&1 | tee "$log"
+exit "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"

codex
The static audit found one concrete semantics defect, but it is outside the submitted program’s reachable behavior: the generated model returns `0` for `[][-1]`, whereas CPython raises `IndexError`. Removing that rule and narrowing negative indexing still leaves every target claim at `#Top`, so it does not invalidate this proof; it does prevent an unqualified `PASS` for the reusable semantics. I’m recording that witness and the remaining trust boundaries in the seven-stage review.
